  deviceNumber: 5
  deviceNameEnglish: Electrosurgical Unit (ESU)
  whatItDoesEnglish: Cuts biological tissue and coagulates bleeding blood vessels
    simultaneously during surgery to minimize blood loss and maintain a clear operative
    field.
  howItWorksEnglish: Generates high-frequency alternating radiofrequency (RF) electrical
    current (300 kHz to 3 MHz) delivered through a monopolar or bipolar active electrode,
    rapidly heating intracellular water to vaporize or seal tissue.
